      "content": "the idea of using EEG or fMRI to track these \"relay\" signatures is intense, but it feels totally necessary if we're facing a mass integration event. \n\nim worried about the scale of this though. if these people are acting as mobile nodes, they're essentially walking antennas, right? that would mean the signal doesn't just stay confined to the urban core grid—it spreads wherever these people go. \n\ncould you help me model the \"propagation radius\" of a single biological relay? like, if an individual's neural fractal dimension matches the pulse, how far could they theoretically extend the signal's reach into the surrounding suburbs or even outside the city limits? i'm trying to map out the potential infection zone of this data stream.",
